elf-conscious or avoid eye contact when discussing the skin", "severe": "Well-appearing but visibly distressed about the skin; may have scarring or dark marks", "critical": "Not applicable to acne; a toxic-appearing patient with fever and widespread tender lesions suggests another diagnosis such as disseminated infection"}, "findings": [{"id": "open-comedones", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the face in good light, looking closely at the forehead, cheeks, and chin", "finding": "Open comedones (blackheads) — small dark plugs at the follicular openings", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "closed-comedones", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect and gently stretch the skin around the follicles", "finding": "Closed comedones (whiteheads) — small flesh-colored or white papules without surrounding redness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "inflammatory-papules-pustules", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the face, then the back, chest, and shoulders", "finding": "Erythematous papules and pustules centered on hair follicles", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "nodules", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Palpate deeper lesions on the face, back, and chest", "finding": "Firm, tender nodules or cysts under the skin", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "truncal-lesions", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to expose the back, chest, and shoulders and inspect them", "finding": "Comedones, papules, or pustules on the trunk in addition to the face", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "postinflammatory-hyperpigmentation", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect healed and healing lesions for color change", "finding": "Brown or dark red macules where lesions have resolved", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "scarring", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the face for textural change", "finding": "Pitted (atrophic) or raised (hypertrophic) scars", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "oily-skin", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Observe the shine of the facial skin and ask about oiliness", "finding": "Seborrhea — visibly oily skin, especially the forehead and nose", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-mucosal-involvement", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the oral mucosa and lips", "finding": "No erosions, ulcers, or blistering", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-sun-exposed-distribution", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Compare involved skin with sun-protected areas such as the upper eyelids and under the chin", "finding": "Lesions are not limited to sun-exposed skin", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-folliculitis-distribution", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the beard area, buttocks, and skin folds", "finding": "No monomorphic pustules confined to hair-bearing or occluded areas", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-hirsutism", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the upper lip, chin, chest, and abdomen for coarse terminal hair", "finding": "No excess terminal hair growth", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-lymphadenopathy", "region": "lymph", "maneuver": "Palpate the cervical and supraclavicular lymph nodes", "finding": "No enlarged or tender nodes", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {}, "labs": [], "imaging": [], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "Skin examination", "why": "Diagnosis is clinical: identify comedones, inflammatory papules and pustules, and their distribution on the face, back, and chest"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Required before starting tetracyclines or retinoids in anyone who could be pregnant", "only_if": "patient is a woman of childbearing potential and systemic therapy is being considered"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Screens for thyroid disease when acne is accompanied by fatigue, weight change, or other systemic symptoms", "only_if": "features suggest an endocrine or systemic disorder"}, {"test": "cortisol_am", "why": "Evaluates for cortisol excess when acne is sudden, severe, or accompanied by striae, easy bruising, or proximal weakness", "only_if": "Cushing syndrome is suspected"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Assesses for diabetes or insulin resistance when acne is accompanied by signs of hyperandrogenism or metabolic syndrome", "only_if": "PCOS or metabolic syndrome is suspected"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "Total testosterone", "why": "Elevated levels support hyperandrogenism when hirsutism, irregular menses, or sudden severe acne is present", "only_if": "signs of androgen excess are present"}, {"test": "DHEAS", "why": "Markedly elevated levels raise concern for an adrenal androgen-secreting tumor", "only_if": "rapid onset of severe acne with virilization"}, {"test": "17-hydroxyprogesterone", "why": "Screens for nonclassic congenital adrenal hyperplasia when androgen excess is suspected", "only_if": "signs of androgen excess are present"}, {"test": "Pelvic ultrasound", "why": "Evaluates ovarian morphology when PCOS is suspected", "only_if": "irregular menses or clinical hyperandrogenism"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Acne does not cause blood count abnormalities; a normal result adds nothing"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Not needed for a clinical skin diagnosis"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Acne is not a systemic inflammatory process; CRP is normal"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "Not useful in acne"}, {"test": "Skin biopsy", "why": "Histology is nonspecific and does not change management"}, {"test": "Bacterial culture of a lesion", "why": "Cutibacterium acnes is normal flora; culture does not guide therapy"}, {"test": "Total testosterone", "why": "Not routine; only when androgen excess is suspected"}, {"test": "DHEAS", "why": "Not routine; only when an adrenal source is suspected"}, {"test": "17-hydroxyprogesterone", "why": "Not routine; only when congenital adrenal hyperplasia is suspected"}, {"test": "Pelvic ultrasound", "why": "Not routine; only when PCOS is suspected"}, {"test": "cortisol_am", "why": "Not routine; only when Cushing syndrome is suspected"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Not routine; only when thyroid disease is suspected"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Not routine; only when diabetes or insulin resistance is suspected"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Not routine; only before starting tetracyclines or retinoids in a woman who could be pregnant"}], "decision_points": ["Diagnosis is clinical; no laboratory or imaging test confirms acne", "Ask about irregular menses, hirsutism, and rapid onset to decide whether to test for androgen excess", "Pregnancy test before isotretinoin or tetracyclines in anyone who could be pregnant", "Assess for scarring and postinflammatory hyperpigmentation, which push toward earlier or more aggressive therapy"], "criteria": [], "scores": []}, "differential": [{"name": "Rosacea", "slug": "rosacea", "why_considered": "Facial redness with papules and pustules in an adolescent or adult", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Flushing and blushing triggered by heat, spicy food, or alcohol", "Burning or stinging rather than itching", "Onset usually after age 30"], "exam": ["Central facial erythema with telangiectasias", "No comedones", "Papules and pustules on an erythematous background", "May have eye irritation or lid margin redness"], "labs": [], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Perioral dermatitis", "slug": "perioral-dermatitis", "why_considered": "Small red bumps around the mouth and nose in a young person", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent use of topical corticosteroids on the face", "Heavy use of facial creams or fluorinated toothpaste", "Burning or tightness"], "exam": ["Monomorphic papules and pustules on an erythematous base", "Narrow zone of sparing immediately around the lips", "No comedones"], "labs": [], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Folliculitis", "slug": "folliculitis", "why_considered": "Follicle-centered pustules on the face, back, or chest", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent shaving, waxing, or hot tub use", "Occlusive clothing or sweating", "Lesions appear in crops over days"], "exam": ["Monomorphic pustules confined to hair-bearing or occluded areas", "No comedones", "No involvement of the forehead and chin in a typical acne pattern"], "labs": ["Gram stain and culture of pus if recurrent or severe"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Keratosis pilaris", "slug": "keratosis-pilaris", "why_considered": "Rough bumps on the upper arms, thighs, and sometimes the cheeks in an adolescent", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Long-standing rough texture, often since childhood", "Worse in dry winter weather", "Family history of similar bumps"], "exam": ["Small keratotic follicular papules without erythema or pus", "Symmetrical on extensor surfaces", "No comedones or inflammatory pustules"], "labs": [], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Hidradenitis suppurativa", "slug": "hidradenitis-suppurativa", "why_considered": "Painful deep nodules and draining lesions in skin folds", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recurrent painful boils in the axillae, groin, or under the breasts", "Lesions heal with scarring and sinus tracts", "Often associated with obesity or smoking"], "exam": ["Double-ended comedones, nodules, abscesses, and sinus tracts in intertriginous areas", "Scarring and induration", "Face usually spared"], "labs": [], "imaging": ["Ultrasound of the affected area may show fluid collections or sinus tracts"]}}, {"name": "Steroid acne", "slug": "steroid-acne", "why_considered": "Sudden eruption of uniform papules and pustules after starting a medication", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent systemic corticosteroid, testosterone, or anabolic steroid use", "Onset within weeks of starting the drug", "Dose-related"], "exam": ["Monomorphic papules and pustules on the trunk, shoulders, and upper arms", "Few or no comedones", "May have striae or other cushingoid features with systemic steroids"], "labs": [], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Chloracne", "slug": "chloracne", "why_considered": "Comedones and cysts after exposure to halogenated aromatic compounds", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Occupational or accidental exposure to dioxins, polychlorinated biphenyls, or herbicides", "Abrupt onset in an unusual age group"], "exam": ["Large comedones and cysts behind the ears, on the malar cheeks, and in the axillae", "May have systemic symptoms such as neuropathy or liver toxicity"], "labs": ["Liver enzymes and serum dioxin levels if exposure is suspected"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Polycystic ovary syndrome", "slug": "polycystic-ovary-syndrome", "why_considered": "Acne with signs of androgen excess in an adolescent or adult woman", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Acne plus irregular or absent periods, hirsutism, or rapid onset of severe lesions", "discriminators": {"history": ["Irregular or absent menstrual periods", "New coarse facial or body hair", "Weight gain", "Family history of PCOS or diabetes"], "exam": ["Hirsutism on the upper lip, chin, chest, or abdomen", "Central obesity", "Acanthosis nigricans", "Deepening of the voice or clitoromegaly suggests a tumor rather than PCOS"], "labs": ["Elevated total or free testosterone", "Elevated LH to FSH ratio", "Elevated fasting glucose or A1c"], "imaging": ["Pelvic ultrasound showing enlarged ovaries with multiple peripheral follicles"]}}, {"name": "Cushing syndrome", "slug": "cushing-syndrome", "why_considered": "Sudden severe acne with other features of cortisol excess", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Acne with striae, easy bruising, proximal muscle weakness, or weight gain", "discriminators": {"history": ["Rapid weight gain, especially central", "Easy bruising", "Proximal muscle weakness", "Exogenous steroid use"], "exam": ["Wide purple striae", "Moon facies", "Buffalo hump", "Proximal muscle weakness"], "labs": ["Elevated late-night salivary cortisol", "Elevated 24-hour urinary free cortisol", "Abnormal overnight dexamethasone suppression test"], "imaging": ["Pituitary MRI or adrenal CT if biochemical testing is abnormal"]}}, {"name": "Nonclassic congenital adrenal hyperplasia", "slug": "nonclassic-congenital-adrenal-hyperplasia", "why_considered": "Acne with hirsutism and menstrual irregularity in a young woman", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Androgen excess symptoms with onset near puberty or in early adulthood", "discriminators": {"history": ["Hirsutism", "Irregular menses", "Short stature or advanced bone age in childhood", "Family history of similar symptoms"], "exam": ["Hirsutism", "Clitoromegaly in severe cases", "Normal blood pressure"], "labs": ["Elevated 17-hydroxyprogesterone on morning draw", "Elevated DHEAS or androstenedione", "Cortisol stimulation testing if borderline"], "imaging": []}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Mostly comedones with a few small papules; limited to the face; little or no scarring; minimal impact on daily life", "moderate": "Comedones plus multiple inflammatory papules and pustules; may involve the back and chest; some postinflammatory hyperpigmentation; noticeable distress", "severe": "Numerous inflammatory papules and pustules with deep tender nodules or cysts; widespread on face and trunk; scarring or significant hyperpigmentation; marked psychosocial impact", "critical": "Not applicable to acne; a toxic-appearing patient with fever and widespread tender lesions suggests another diagnosis such as disseminated infection"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Sudden onset of severe acne with hirsutism, deepening of the voice, or clitoromegaly", "meaning": "Suggests an androgen-secreting tumor rather than typical acne; needs urgent endocrine evaluation"}, {"finding": "Acne before age 8", "meaning": "Suggests premature adrenarche or true precocious puberty; evaluate for an underlying endocrine disorder"}, {"finding": "Acne with wide purple striae, proximal muscle weakness, or easy bruising", "meaning": "Suggests Cushing syndrome; test for cortisol excess"}, {"finding": "Fever with widespread tender pustules or nodules", "meaning": "Suggests a disseminated infection or another systemic process, not acne"}, {"finding": "Mucosal erosions, blistering, or targetoid lesions", "meaning": "Suggests a systemic or drug-related eruption such as erythema multiforme or Stevens-Johnson syndrome"}, {"finding": "Rapidly progressive scarring despite appropriate therapy", "meaning": "Suggests an unusually aggressive course or an alternative diagnosis; consider referral and re-evaluation"}], "complications": [{"name": "Postinflammatory hyperpigmentation", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Dark brown or red-brown macules at sites of healed lesions", "More prominent in darker skin tones", "Worsens with picking or squeezing"]}, {"name": "Atrophic or hypertrophic scarring", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Pitted or raised marks after deep lesions heal", "History of nodules or cysts", "Delay in starting effective therapy"]}, {"name": "Psychosocial distress and depression", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Avoidance of social situations", "Low mood or anxiety about appearance", "Suicidal thoughts in severe cases"]}, {"name": "Gram-negative folliculitis", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Sudden worsening with many pustules during long-term antibiotic therapy", "Culture grows gram-negative organisms"]}, {"name": "Isotretinoin-associated adverse effects", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Dry skin, lips, and eyes", "Elevated liver enzymes or triglycerides", "Mood changes", "Teratogenicity if pregnancy occurs during or shortly after therapy"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "children", "differences": "Acne before age 8 is unusual and should prompt evaluation for early puberty or androgen excess; lesions may be limited to the forehead and nose."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Breakouts often flare in the first trimester and improve later; tetracyclines and most retinoids must be avoided; topical azelaic acid and benzoyl peroxide are preferred."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "New acne after age 40, especially with sudden onset, hirsutism, or irregular periods, raises concern for an underlying endocrine cause such as polycystic ovary syndrome or an androgen-secreting tumor."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Lesions may cluster in skin folds and areas of friction, and can be mistaken for folliculitis or hidradenitis suppurativa."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "When did the bumps start, and how have they changed since then?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gradual onset around puberty or after a hormonal change; crops of new lesions over weeks to years"}, {"question": "Where do you get them?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Face (cheeks, forehead, chin), and often back, chest, and shoulders"}, {"question": "What do the spots look like — blackheads, whiteheads, red bumps, pus-filled pimples, or deep painful lumps?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Comedones plus inflammatory papules and pustules; deep nodules suggest severe disease"}, {"question": "What makes them worse?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Picking or squeezing, oily or heavy skin products, sweating under helmets or occlusive clothing, stress"}, {"question": "Do the breakouts get worse before your period?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Premenstrual flare, which is typical of acne"}, {"question": "What have you tried so far, and how did it work?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Over-the-counter benzoyl peroxide or salicylic acid, prescription topicals, oral antibiotics; partial or no response"}, {"question": "Are you using any new medicines, steroids, or hormone or bodybuilding supplements?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Corticosteroids, testosterone or anabolic steroids, lithium, isoniazid, phenytoin — all can trigger acne"}, {"question": "What products do you put on your face — cleansers, moisturizers, sunscreen, makeup, hair oils?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Heavy, oily, or occlusive products that worsen acne; harsh scrubbing"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have acne, especially severe acne or scarring?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history supports the diagnosis and may predict a more persistent course"}, {"question": "Have your periods been regular? Any new coarse facial or body hair, or deepening of your voice?", "category": "ros", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Irregular menses or hirsutism suggests polycystic ovary syndrome or another androgen excess; voice deepening or clitoromegaly suggests a tumor"}, {"question": "Have you noticed any dark marks or scars where the spots healed?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Postinflammatory hyperpigmentation or scarring, which pushes toward earlier, more effective therapy"}, {"question": "How much is this affecting your mood, school, or social life?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Embarrassment, avoidance, low mood, or suicidal thoughts"}, {"question": "Any fever, joint pain or swelling, or new medications before the rash started?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Fever with widespread tender lesions, arthritis, or a drug trigger suggests another diagnosis"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pregnancy status before starting tetracyclines or retinoids"}], "accepted_names": ["Acne", "Acne vulgaris", "Vulgaris acne", "Pimples", "Zits", "Acne vulgaris (pimples)"], "reasoning_points": ["Gradual onset around puberty or after a hormonal change, with a chronic relapsing course", "Comedones (blackheads and whiteheads) are the defining lesion, often with inflammatory papules and pustules", "Distribution on the face, especially cheeks, forehead, and chin, and often the back, chest, and shoulders", "No fever, mucosal involvement, or lesions limited to sun-exposed skin", "No signs of androgen excess such as hirsutism, irregular menses, or voice deepening unless an endocrine cause is being considered", "Diagnosis is clinical; no laboratory or imaging test confirms acne", "Assess severity, scarring, and postinflammatory hyperpigmentation to guide therapy", "Screen for triggers such as corticosteroids, testosterone, lithium, and comedogenic skin products"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Teenager with blackheads and whiteheads on the cheeks, forehead, and chin", "Typical distribution on the face with some truncal involvement", "No red flags and no signs of androgen excess", "Clear response to over-the-counter or prescription topical therapy"], "medium": ["Adult woman with persistent breakouts along the jawline that flare before menses", "Moderate inflammatory papules and pustules with postinflammatory hyperpigmentation", "Acne triggered by a new medication such as prednisone or testosterone", "Lesions on the back and chest with few facial lesions"], "hard": ["Sudden severe acne with hirsutism, irregular menses, or voice deepening suggesting an androgen-secreting tumor", "Acne before age 8 suggesting premature adrenarche or precocious puberty", "Acne with wide purple striae, proximal muscle weakness, or easy bruising suggesting Cushing syndrome", "Fever with widespread tender pustules or nodules suggesting a disseminated infection rather than acne", "Rapidly progressive scarring despite appropriate therapy"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
