oidism: no profile yet", "differential arrhythmia: no profile yet", "differential pulmonary-embolism: no profile yet", "differential substance-induced-anxiety: no profile yet", "differential major-depressive-disorder: no profile yet", "differential generalized-anxiety-disorder: no profile yet", "differential panic-disorder: no profile yet", "differential social-anxiety-disorder: no profile yet", "differential irritable-bowel-syndrome: no profile yet"]}, "review": {"status": "pending"}}, "patient": {"age": {"typical_min": 18, "typical_max": 60, "peak": "20s–30s", "possible_min": 6, "possible_max": 90}, "sex": "female_predominant", "demographics": ["Generalized anxiety and phobias are more common in women; social anxiety is roughly equal between men and women", "Often first seen in primary care rather than by a mental health clinician"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Family history of anxiety or another mental disorder", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Traumatic or stressful life events, including in childhood", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Shy, withdrawn temperament or behavioral inhibition in new situations", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Ongoing life stress such as job, school, financial, or relationship strain", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Heavy caffeine or stimulant use", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Female sex", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Depression", "Other anxiety disorders", "Substance use, especially alcohol or sedatives", "Irritable bowel syndrome", "Chronic pain or headache syndromes", "Thyroid disease", "Asthma or other chronic medical illness"], "family_history": ["Anxiety disorder in a parent or sibling", "Depression or another mental disorder in the family"], "social_history": ["Recent or ongoing stressors at work, school, or home", "Limited social support or recent loss", "Heavy caffeine intake", "Alcohol or cannabis use to calm down"], "exposures": ["Stimulants such as caffeine, nicotine, or decongestants", "Stressful or traumatic events"], "risk_medications": ["albuterol", "levothyroxine", "prednisone", "methylphenidate", "amphetamine", "bupropion"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I can't stop worrying about everything", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "I feel tense and on edge all the time", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My heart races and I feel like something bad is going to happen", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I can't sleep because my mind won't shut off", "frequency": "common"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual, often building over months; many patients date it to a stressful period or a major life change", "duration": "Weeks to years; by the time it is diagnosed, symptoms have usually been present most days for at least several months", "progression": "Chronic and fluctuating, worse during stressful periods and better during calmer ones; it rarely resolves on its own without treatment", "location": "Not localized; described as a whole-body feeling of tension", "radiation": "Not applicable", "quality": "Persistent worry that feels hard to control, with a physical sense of restlessness and tension", "severity": "Mild to moderate for most; can be severe enough to interfere with work, school, sleep, and relationships", "timing": "Most days, often worse in the evening or when trying to fall asleep", "aggravating": ["Stress at work, school, or home", "Caffeine", "Poor sleep", "Conflict or bad news", "Crowds or being far from home"], "relieving": ["Talking to someone supportive", "Exercise", "Quiet, familiar surroundings", "Alcohol or other substances (patients often report this, though it worsens things over time)"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Restlessness or feeling keyed up", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Trouble falling or staying asleep", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Muscle tension, especially neck, shoulders, or jaw", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Trouble concentrating or mind going blank", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Irritability", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Feeling easily tired", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Palpitations or a pounding heartbeat", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath or a smothering feeling", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dizziness or lightheadedness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Sweating, trembling, or a churning stomach", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Avoiding situations that trigger the worry", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Headaches", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Chest pain that comes on with exertion and resolves with rest", "Fainting or loss of consciousness", "Weight loss despite normal appetite", "Heat intolerance with tremor and weight loss", "New focal weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking", "Hearing voices or having thoughts others are out to get them", "Using a substance every day and feeling sick without it", "Symptoms that only occur after a specific substance or medication"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Feeling tired", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Feeling keyed up or restless", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fever", "Night sweats"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Palpitations", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Racing heartbeat during worry", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Chest pain with exertion", "Fainting", "Swelling in the legs"], "argues_against": ["Chest pain that reliably comes with exertion and eases with rest"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Shortness of breath when anxious", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Feeling like I can't get a full breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Cough", "Wheezing", "Coughing up blood"], "argues_against": ["Shortness of breath with wheeze that responds to an inhaler"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Butterflies or churning stomach", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Loose stools when stressed", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Vomiting blood", "Black or bloody stools", "Trouble swallowing solid food"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Muscle tension in the neck and shoulders", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Jaw clenching or grinding", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Joint swelling", "New weakness in an arm or leg"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [{"text": "Headaches", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dizziness or lightheadedness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Trembling hands", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Fainting", "Seizures", "Numbness or weakness on one side", "Trouble speaking"], "argues_against": ["Sudden focal neurologic deficit"]}, {"system": "psychiatric", "positives": [{"text": "Worry that is hard to control", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Feeling on edge", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Trouble concentrating", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Irritability", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Avoiding things that trigger the worry", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low mood or loss of interest", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Hearing voices", "Thoughts of harming myself or others", "Seeing things others don't see", "Feeling that others are plotting against me"], "argues_against": ["Psychosis", "Mania with decreased need for sleep and racing thoughts"]}, {"system": "endocrine", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Heat or cold intolerance", "Excessive thirst and urination"], "argues_against": ["Thyroid disease as the cause"]}, {"system": "hematologic", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Easy bruising or bleeding"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Young children often show anxiety as stomachaches, headaches, clinginess, tantrums, or refusal to go to school rather than describing worry in words.", "missing_classic_features": ["Ability to describe excessive worry", "Insight that the worry is out of proportion"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Anxiety often shows up as physical complaints, poor sleep, or agitation, and is frequently mixed with depression or early cognitive changes; medical causes and medication side effects are more likely.", "missing_classic_features": ["Reporting worry as the main problem", "Clear onset during a stressful life period"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Worry often centers on the pregnancy, the baby's health, and childbirth, and physical symptoms overlap with normal pregnancy changes.", "missing_classic_features": ["Symptoms clearly separate from pregnancy-related body changes"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Alert, well-groomed, cooperative; appears mildly tense but comfortable", "moderate": "Restless, fidgeting, wringing hands, leg bouncing; speech may be rapid", "severe": "Markedly agitated or tremulous, diaphoretic, visibly distressed, may have trouble staying seated", "critical": "Extreme agitation or panic, hyperventilating, diaphoretic, appears terrified; unable to participate in exam"}, "findings": [{"id": "apprehensive-affect", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Observe the patient's demeanor and affect during the interview", "finding": "Anxious, apprehensive, or tense affect; appears worried or on edge", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "psychomotor-restlessness", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Observe the patient's motor activity during the visit", "finding": "Restlessness, fidgeting, hand wringing, foot tapping, or difficulty sitting still", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "speech-normal", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Listen to the patient's spontaneous speech", "finding": "Speech is normal in rate, rhythm, and volume without pressured quality or flight of ideas", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "thought-process-linear", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Assess the organization and flow of the patient's thoughts during history", "finding": "Thought process is linear and goal-directed without loosening of associations", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-psychosis", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Ask about hearing voices, seeing things others do not, or feeling that others are plotting against them", "finding": "No hallucinations or delusions", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "no-suicidal-ideation", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Ask directly about thoughts of harming oneself or others", "finding": "No suicidal or homicidal ideation, intent, or plan", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "intact-orientation", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Assess orientation to person, place, time, and situation", "finding": "Oriented to person, place, time, and situation; attention and concentration grossly intact", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "neck-muscle-tension", "region": "musculoskeletal", "maneuver": "Palpate the trapezius and paraspinal muscles of the neck and shoulders", "finding": "Muscle tightness or tenderness in the neck and shoulders", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "tremor", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to hold both arms outstretched with fingers spread", "finding": "Fine postural tremor of the hands", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "diaphoresis", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Observe and palpate the skin", "finding": "Cool, clammy, or sweaty palms and skin", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-thyroid-enlargement", "region": "neck", "maneuver": "Palpate the thyroid gland while the patient swallows", "finding": "No goiter or thyroid nodule", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-exophthalmos", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the eyes for proptosis and lid lag", "finding": "No exophthalmos or lid lag", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "cardiac-normal", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the heart in the sitting and supine positions", "finding": "Regular rate and rhythm without murmurs, rubs, or gallops", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "lung-normal", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lungs bilaterally", "finding": "Clear breath sounds without wheezes, crackles, or prolonged expiration", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-focal-neuro-deficit", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Perform a focused neurologic exam including cranial nerves, strength, sensation, and coordination", "finding": "No focal motor, sensory, or cranial nerve deficits", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-goiter", "region": "neck", "maneuver": "Inspect the neck for visible thyroid enlargement", "finding": "No visible goiter", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {"hr": {"mild": {"min": 70, "max": 95}, "moderate": {"min": 85, "max": 110}, "severe": {"min": 100, "max": 130}, "critical": {"min": 110, "max": 150}}, "rr": {"moderate": {"min": 16, "max": 22}, "severe": {"min": 20, "max": 28}, "critical": {"min": 24, "max": 36}}, "sbp": {"moderate": {"min": 110, "max": 140}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 150}, "critical": {"min": 130, "max": 160}}, "dbp": {"moderate": {"min": 70, "max": 88}, "severe": {"min": 75, "max": 95}, "critical": {"min": 80, "max": 100}}, "spo2": {"severe": {"min": 94, "max": 98}, "critical": {"min": 90, "max": 96}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "tsh", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 0.1, "max": 0.35}, "moderate": {"min": 0.05, "max": 0.3}, "severe": {"min": 0.01, "max": 0.2}, "critical": {"min": 0.01, "max": 0.1}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Hyperthyroidism can mimic anxiety with palpitations, tremor, heat intolerance, and weight loss; a suppressed TSH with high free T4 points to thyroid disease rather than an anxiety disorder."}, {"test_id": "ft4", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.9, "max": 3.0}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 4.5}, "critical": {"min": 3.0, "max": 6.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Ordered when TSH is low to confirm thyrotoxicosis."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 60, "max": 69}, "severe": {"min": 45, "max": 59}, "critical": {"min": 30, "max": 44}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Hypoglycemia can cause palpitations, tremor, and a sense of dread; check if symptoms occur fasting or with diabetes treatment."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Negative. In a patient who could be pregnant, a positive result changes the differential and limits medication choices."}, {"test_id": "cortisol_am", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 26, "max": 35}, "severe": {"min": 30, "max": 45}, "critical": {"min": 35, "max": 60}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Only when features suggest Cushing syndrome (weight gain, striae, easy bruising, proximal weakness)."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 7.5, "max": 10.0}, "critical": {"min": 8.5, "max": 12.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Not a cause of anxiety; screens for diabetes when symptoms overlap or before starting some medications."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.5}, "moderate": {"min": 1.4, "max": 2.0}, "severe": {"min": 1.8, "max": 3.0}, "critical": {"min": 2.5, "max": 5.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Baseline renal function before starting a medication that is renally cleared."}, {"test_id": "na", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 131, "max": 134}, "moderate": {"min": 126, "max": 130}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 125}, "critical": {"min": 110, "max": 119}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Hyponatremia can present with confusion, restlessness, or anxiety; consider if the patient takes a diuretic or SSRI."}, {"test_id": "ca", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 10.3, "max": 11.0}, "moderate": {"min": 11.0, "max": 12.0}, "severe": {"min": 12.0, "max": 14.0}, "critical": {"min": 13.0, "max": 16.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Hypercalcemia can cause anxiety, confusion, and fatigue."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rate", "finding": "Sinus tachycardia", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Normal sinus rhythm", "frequency": "common"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "No ischemic ST-segment changes, no arrhythmia, and no conduction abnormality", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, "imaging": [{"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Normal heart size and clear lungs", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "No acute cardiopulmonary process", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, {"study": "CT pulmonary angiogram", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Only when pulmonary embolism is suspected (sudden dyspnea, pleuritic chest pain, hypoxia, tachycardia, or a positive D-dimer)", "findings": [{"text": "No filling defect in the pulmonary arteries", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, {"study": "CT head without contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Only when a structural brain cause is suspected (new focal deficit, seizure, or altered mental status)", "findings": [{"text": "No acute intracranial abnormality", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "tsh", "why": "Thyroid disease is the most common medical mimic of anxiety"}, {"test": "cbc", "why": "Anemia can cause palpitations, fatigue, and dyspnea"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Electrolyte and glucose abnormalities can mimic anxiety"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Pregnancy changes the differential and treatment choices", "only_if": "the patient could be pregnant"}, {"test": "Electrocardiogram (ECG)", "why": "Evaluates palpitations, tachycardia, or chest symptoms and looks for arrhythmia", "only_if": "palpitations, chest pain, or tachycardia are prominent"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Psychological evaluation", "why": "Structured assessment of worry, panic attacks, avoidance, and functional impairment establishes the diagnosis and the specific anxiety disorder"}], "supporting": [{"test": "ft4", "why": "Confirms thyrotoxicosis when TSH is low", "only_if": "TSH is suppressed"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Screens for diabetes when symptoms overlap or before starting medication", "only_if": "diabetes is a concern"}, {"test": "cr", "why": "Baseline renal function before starting a renally cleared medication", "only_if": "pharmacotherapy is planned"}, {"test": "cortisol_am", "why": "Evaluates for Cushing syndrome", "only_if": "features suggest cortisol excess"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Screens for a urinary cause when urinary frequency or dysuria is prominent", "only_if": "urinary symptoms are present"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "CT pulmonary angiogram", "why": "Not needed unless pulmonary embolism is suspected", "only_if": "pulmonary embolism is suspected (sudden dyspnea, pleuritic chest pain, hypoxia, or tachycardia)"}, {"test": "CT head without contrast", "why": "Not needed without focal neurologic findings, seizure, or altered mental status", "only_if": "a structural brain cause is suspected (new focal deficit, seizure, or altered mental status)"}, {"test": "d_dimer", "why": "No role in the routine workup of anxiety"}, {"test": "hs_tnt", "why": "Not indicated unless chest pain suggests acute coronary syndrome"}, {"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Not routine; reserve for suspected pulmonary disease", "only_if": "respiratory symptoms or an abnormal lung exam suggest pulmonary disease"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "No role in the routine workup of anxiety"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "No role in the routine workup of anxiety"}, {"test": "lipase", "why": "Not indicated unless abdominal pain suggests pancreatitis"}, {"test": "b12", "why": "Not routine; consider only if neurologic findings or a dietary deficiency is suspected"}, {"test": "ferritin", "why": "Not routine; consider only if anemia is found on CBC"}], "decision_points": ["Rule out medical mimics (thyroid disease, arrhythmia, substance or medication effects) before diagnosing a primary anxiety disorder", "Ask directly about suicidal ideation and safety at every visit", "Pregnancy test before starting medication in anyone who could be pregnant", "Do not order chest imaging or cardiac testing unless the history or exam points to a cardiopulmonary cause"], "criteria": [{"name": "Generalized anxiety disorder", "summary": "Excessive worry that is hard to control, occurring more days than not for at least 6 months, with at least three of: restlessness or feeling keyed up, being easily fatigued, trouble concentrating, irritability, muscle tension, and sleep disturbance. The worry causes distress or impairment and is not due to a substance, medication, or another medical condition."}, {"name": "Panic disorder", "summary": "Recurrent unexpected panic attacks followed by at least one month of persistent concern about further attacks or their consequences, or a maladaptive change in behavior related to the attacks."}, {"name": "Social anxiety disorder", "summary": "Marked fear or anxiety about one or more social situations in which the person may be scrutinized, with fear of showing anxiety symptoms or being negatively evaluated. The situations are avoided or endured with intense fear, and the fear is out of proportion to the actual threat."}], "scores": ["gad_7", "phq_9", "panic_severity_scale"]}, "differential": [{"name": "Hyperthyroidism", "slug": "hyperthyroidism", "why_considered": "Palpitations, tremor, restlessness, heat intolerance, and weight loss overlap closely with anxiety", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Palpitations with tremor, heat intolerance, weight loss, or a goiter", "discriminators": {"history": ["Weight loss despite a good appetite", "Heat intolerance and increased sweating", "Diarrhea or frequent stools", "Symptoms that are constant rather than tied to stress"], "exam": ["Goiter or thyroid nodule", "Lid lag or exophthalmos", "Warm, moist skin", "Fine tremor that persists at rest"], "labs": ["Suppressed TSH with elevated free T4 or T3"]}}, {"name": "Cardiac arrhythmia", "slug": "arrhythmia", "why_considered": "Palpitations and a racing heartbeat are common anxiety complaints, and paroxysmal arrhythmias can be mistaken for panic attacks", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Palpitations that start and stop abruptly, syncope, or a family history of sudden death", "discriminators": {"history": ["Abrupt onset and offset of palpitations", "Palpitations at rest or during sleep", "Near-fainting or fainting", "Known structural heart disease"], "exam": ["Irregular pulse or a rate that does not match the reported distress", "Signs of heart failure such as jugular venous distension or edema"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and CBC"], "imaging": ["ECG showing atrial fibrillation, supraventricular tachycardia, or another arrhythmia", "Echocardiogram showing structural disease when indicated"]}}, {"name": "Pulmonary embolism", "slug": "pulmonary-embolism", "why_considered": "Sudden shortness of breath, chest tightness, and tachycardia can look like a panic attack", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Sudden dyspnea with pleuritic chest pain, hypoxia, or tachycardia out of proportion to distress", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden onset rather than a build-up over months", "Pleuritic chest pain worse with deep breath", "Recent surgery, immobility, or a prior clot", "Active cancer or estrogen use"], "exam": ["Tachycardia with clear lungs", "Hypoxia on pulse oximetry", "Unilateral leg swelling or calf tenderness"], "labs": ["Elevated D-dimer", "Respiratory alkalosis with low PaCO2"], "imaging": ["Filling defect in the pulmonary arteries on CT pulmonary angiogram"]}}, {"name": "Substance or medication-induced anxiety", "slug": "substance-induced-anxiety", "why_considered": "Caffeine, stimulants, decongestants, steroids, and alcohol or sedative withdrawal all produce anxiety symptoms", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Symptoms that began or worsened after a substance, medication, or a period of heavy use", "discriminators": {"history": ["Heavy caffeine, energy drink, or stimulant use", "New medication such as albuterol, prednisone, or levothyroxine", "Alcohol or sedative use with tremor and sweats when stopping", "Temporal link between the substance and the symptoms"], "exam": ["Tremor, diaphoresis, and tachycardia during withdrawal", "Agitation or altered mental status"], "labs": ["Urine drug screen positive for stimulants or other substances", "Normal TSH and CBC"]}}, {"name": "Major depressive disorder", "slug": "major-depressive-disorder", "why_considered": "Depression and anxiety commonly occur together, and both cause poor sleep, poor concentration, and irritability", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Persistent low mood or loss of interest most of the day", "Guilt, hopelessness, or thoughts of death", "Anxiety symptoms that began after the mood symptoms"], "exam": ["Flat or sad affect rather than tense and apprehensive", "Psychomotor slowing rather than restlessness"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and CBC"]}}, {"name": "Generalized anxiety disorder", "slug": "generalized-anxiety-disorder", "why_considered": "The index condition itself; the differential workup must confirm that the worry is not better explained by another disorder", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Excessive worry about several areas that is hard to control, more days than not for at least 6 months", "At least three of restlessness, easy fatigue, poor concentration, irritability, muscle tension, and sleep disturbance", "No discrete panic attacks or a single feared situation"], "exam": ["Anxious, apprehensive affect with normal speech and thought process", "No focal neurologic deficit"], "labs": ["Normal TSH, CBC, and metabolic panel"]}}, {"name": "Panic disorder", "slug": "panic-disorder", "why_considered": "Recurrent unexpected panic attacks with fear of further attacks can be mistaken for generalized anxiety", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Discrete attacks that peak within minutes", "Intense fear of dying, losing control, or going crazy during attacks", "At least a month of worry about further attacks or avoidance"], "exam": ["Symptoms are episodic and the exam is normal between attacks"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and ECG"]}}, {"name": "Social anxiety disorder", "slug": "social-anxiety-disorder", "why_considered": "Fear of scrutiny and avoidance of social situations overlaps with generalized worry", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Fear limited to social or performance situations", "Fear of embarrassment or negative evaluation", "Avoidance of speaking, eating, or performing in front of others"], "exam": ["Anxiety appears only when discussing social situations"]}}, {"name": "Irritable bowel syndrome", "slug": "irritable-bowel-syndrome", "why_considered": "Anxiety and IBS frequently coexist, and both cause abdominal discomfort and altered stool habits", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recurrent abdominal pain related to defecation", "Change in stool frequency or form", "Symptoms relieved by defecation"], "exam": ["Mild diffuse abdominal tenderness without peritoneal signs"], "labs": ["Normal CBC, CRP, and celiac serology when ordered"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Worry most days that is bothersome but does not limit work, school, or relationships; sleep and appetite are largely intact", "moderate": "Worry is hard to control and causes clear distress or impairment at work, school, or home; sleep disturbance, muscle tension, and avoidance are present", "severe": "Pervasive worry with marked functional impairment, frequent panic symptoms, poor sleep, and difficulty leaving home or completing daily tasks", "critical": "Extreme agitation or a prolonged panic state with hyperventilation, diaphoresis, and inability to participate in the exam; assess for suicidal ideation and consider a medical cause"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Suicidal ideation, intent, or plan", "meaning": "A psychiatric emergency requiring immediate safety planning and evaluation"}, {"finding": "New focal weakness, numbness, trouble speaking, or seizure", "meaning": "Suggests a structural neurologic cause rather than a primary anxiety disorder"}, {"finding": "Sudden dyspnea with pleuritic chest pain, hypoxia, or tachycardia out of proportion to distress", "meaning": "Consider pulmonary embolism or another acute cardiopulmonary cause"}, {"finding": "Palpitations with syncope or near-syncope", "meaning": "Consider an arrhythmia or structural heart disease"}, {"finding": "Weight loss, heat intolerance, or tremor with a goiter", "meaning": "Consider hyperthyroidism"}, {"finding": "Symptoms that began after a substance, medication, or during withdrawal", "meaning": "Consider substance- or medication-induced anxiety"}], "complications": [{"name": "Major depressive disorder", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Persistent low mood or loss of interest", "Guilt or hopelessness", "Suicidal ideation"]}, {"name": "Substance use disorder", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Alcohol or sedative use to calm down", "Increasing tolerance or withdrawal symptoms"]}, {"name": "Functional impairment and lost productivity", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Missed work or school", "Avoidance of social or occupational activities"]}, {"name": "Insomnia", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Trouble falling or staying asleep", "Daytime fatigue and poor concentration"]}, {"name": "Suicidal ideation or attempt", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Expressed hopelessness", "Prior attempt", "Access to lethal means"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "children", "differences": "Young children often show anxiety as stomachaches, headaches, clinginess, tantrums, or refusal to attend school rather than describing worry in words; involve parents and school in the assessment."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Anxiety often presents as physical complaints, poor sleep, or agitation and is frequently mixed with depression or early cognitive changes; medical causes and medication side effects are more likely, so review the medication list carefully."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Worry often centers on the pregnancy, the baby's health, and childbirth, and physical symptoms overlap with normal pregnancy changes; check pregnancy status before starting medication and weigh risks and benefits with the patient."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Tell me about your worry — what kinds of things do you worry about, and how much of the day is it on your mind?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Worry about several different areas (health, money, work, family) that is excessive and hard to control, present most days"}, {"question": "How long has this been going on?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Most days for at least 6 months; shorter duration or a clear recent trigger points elsewhere"}, {"question": "Is the worry there all the time, or does it come in sudden attacks that peak within minutes?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Continuous background worry suggests generalized anxiety; discrete attacks peaking within minutes suggest panic attacks"}, {"question": "Does the worry or the physical symptoms get in the way of work, school, or your relationships?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Distress or functional impairment, which is required to call it a disorder rather than a normal reaction"}, {"question": "How is your sleep?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Trouble falling or staying asleep because the mind will not shut off"}, {"question": "Do you feel restless, keyed up, or on edge?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Restlessness or feeling wound up"}, {"question": "Do you notice muscle tension, especially in your neck, shoulders, or jaw?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Muscle tension, jaw clenching, or grinding"}, {"question": "How is your concentration?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Trouble concentrating or the mind going blank"}, {"question": "Do you feel irritable or easily tired?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Irritability and easy fatigability"}, {"question": "Do you have palpitations, shortness of breath, dizziness, sweating, or stomach upset?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Physical symptoms of anxiety; also helps separate a primary anxiety disorder from a medical mimic"}, {"question": "Are there situations you now avoid because of the worry?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Avoidance of crowds, driving, social situations, or leaving home"}, {"question": "Have you been feeling down, hopeless, or lost interest in things you used to enjoy?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Coexisting depression, which is common and changes treatment"}, {"question": "Have you had any thoughts of hurting yourself or that you would be better off dead?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Suicidal ideation, intent, or plan — a psychiatric emergency"}, {"question": "Do you hear voices, see things others do not, or feel that people are plotting against you?", "category": "ros", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; psychosis points to a different diagnosis"}, {"question": "Have you had any new weakness, numbness, trouble speaking, or a seizure?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; focal neurologic findings suggest a structural cause"}, {"question": "Have you ever had chest pain with exertion that eases with rest, or fainting?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests a cardiac cause rather than anxiety"}, {"question": "Have you had weight loss despite a normal appetite, heat intolerance, or diarrhea?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests hyperthyroidism"}, {"question": "How much caffeine do you take in — coffee, tea, energy drinks, soda?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Heavy caffeine or stimulant use that could be driving the symptoms"}, {"question": "How much alcohol, cannabis, or other substances do you use, and do you use them to calm down?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Substance use or withdrawal as a cause, or self-medication"}, {"question": "What medications and supplements do you take, including any inhalers or steroids?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Albuterol, levothyroxine, prednisone, methylphenidate, amphetamine, or bupropion that can cause or worsen anxiety"}, {"question": "Has a doctor ever told you that you have a thyroid problem or a heart rhythm problem?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Thyroid disease or arrhythmia as a medical mimic"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have anxiety, depression, or another mental health condition?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history of anxiety or another mental disorder"}, {"question": "What has been going on in your life lately — work, school, money, relationships, or any losses?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Ongoing stressors or a recent traumatic event"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pregnancy status, which changes the differential and limits medication choices"}], "accepted_names": ["Anxiety", "Anxiety disorder", "Generalized anxiety disorder", "GAD", "Anxiety disorder, unspecified"], "reasoning_points": ["Excessive worry about several areas that the patient finds hard to control, present more days than not for at least 6 months", "At least three of restlessness, easy fatigue, poor concentration, irritability, muscle tension, and sleep disturbance", "The worry causes distress or clear impairment at work, school, or in relationships", "Anxious, apprehensive affect with normal speech, linear thought process, and no psychosis", "Suicidal ideation asked about directly and documented", "Medical mimics excluded: normal TSH, CBC, and metabolic panel; no goiter, tremor at rest, or focal neurologic deficit", "Substances and medications reviewed as possible causes (caffeine, stimulants, decongestants, steroids, alcohol or sedative withdrawal)", "Coexisting depression screened for with a validated tool such as the GAD-7 and PHQ-9"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young adult with months of worry about several areas, trouble sleeping, and muscle tension", "Classic anxious affect with normal speech and thought process", "Normal TSH and no medical red flags", "Clear functional impairment described in the patient's own words"], "medium": ["Prominent physical symptoms (palpitations, shortness of breath, dizziness) that raise a cardiac or pulmonary concern", "Heavy caffeine or stimulant use that could explain the symptoms", "Anxiety mixed with depression, making it unclear which came first", "Older adult whose anxiety shows up as physical complaints and poor sleep"], "hard": ["Symptoms that began after a new medication such as albuterol, prednisone, or levothyroxine", "Palpitations that start and stop abruptly or occur at rest, suggesting an arrhythmia", "Sudden dyspnea with pleuritic chest pain and tachycardia out of proportion to distress", "Child who presents with stomachaches, headaches, or school refusal rather than describing worry", "Patient with a goiter, weight loss, and heat intolerance suggesting hyperthyroidism"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
