tory pain without classic migration to the right lower quadrant"], "exam": ["Tenderness may be less focal", "No peritoneal signs"], "labs": ["White count normal or mildly elevated"], "imaging": ["Enlarged mesenteric lymph nodes with a normal appendix on ultrasound or CT"]}}, {"name": "Crohn disease", "slug": "crohns-disease", "why_considered": "Right lower quadrant pain from terminal ileitis can mimic appendicitis.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Weeks to months of diarrhea", "Weight loss", "Prior similar episodes", "Family history of inflammatory bowel disease"], "exam": ["Right lower quadrant tenderness without acute peritoneal signs", "Possible perianal findings"], "labs": ["Anemia", "Elevated inflammatory markers", "White count may be normal"], "imaging": ["Terminal ileum wall thickening and inflammation on CT or MRI enterography"]}}, {"name": "Diverticulitis", "slug": "diverticulitis", "why_considered": "Left or lower abdominal pain with fever and leukocytosis; can present on the right in some patients.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Older adult", "Left lower quadrant pain more typical", "Prior episodes of diverticulitis", "Constipation or change in bowel habit"], "exam": ["Left lower quadrant tenderness", "Possible palpable mass"], "labs": ["Leukocytosis", "Elevated CRP"], "imaging": ["Diverticula with pericolic fat stranding on CT"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Early, uncomplicated appendicitis: less than 24 hours of symptoms, localized right lower quadrant tenderness, low-grade or no fever, mild leukocytosis.", "moderate": "Established, uncomplicated appendicitis: clear migration of pain, guarding, fever, and marked leukocytosis.", "severe": "Perforated appendicitis with a localized abscess or phlegmon: high fever, persistent pain, palpable mass, and marked leukocytosis.", "critical": "Free perforation with generalized peritonitis and sepsis: rigid abdomen, hypotension, tachycardia, and altered men