ttacks can build gradually or come on suddenly after a trigger.", "location": "Chest", "quality": "Whistling or musical sound when breathing out, with a sensation of chest tightness and air hunger", "severity": "Mild to severe; children between episodes may feel completely normal, while during an attack they may be unable to speak in full sentences or feed normally", "timing": "Often worse at night and in the early morning; frequently triggered by exercise, cold air, or a cold", "aggravating": ["Exercise", "Cold air", "Tobacco smoke", "Dust or dusting/vacuuming", "Pets", "Pollen season", "Colds or flu", "Laughing or crying hard"], "relieving": ["Resting", "Sitting upright", "Fresh air", "Reliever inhaler (albuterol)", "Nebulized medicine in the office or emergency department"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Cough, especially at night", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath with activity", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest tightness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Runny or stuffy nose and sneezing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Itchy, watery eyes", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Trouble feeding or sucking in infants", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Feeling tired or irritable", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dark circles under the eyes", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Fever as the main problem", "Wheezing that started suddenly while eating or playing with a small object", "Wheezing present since birth without symptom-free periods", "Frequent spitting up or choking with feeds", "Poor weight gain or failure to thrive", "Chronic productive cough with blood", "Night sweats or weight loss", "Symptoms that only occur with one specific food"]}, "ros": [{"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Wheezing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Cough, worse at night", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest tightness", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Coughing up blood", "Wheezing that started suddenly while eating or playing with a small toy", "Wheezing since birth without any symptom-free periods"], "argues_against": ["Foreign body aspiration", "Structural airway problem"]}, {"system": "ent", "positives": [{"text": "Runny or stuffy nose", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sneezing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Itchy, watery eyes", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Chronic purulent nasal discharge", "Facial pain"], "argues_against": ["Chronic sinusitis as the sole cause"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Feeling tired", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Irritability", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Weight loss", "Night sweats", "Failure to thrive"], "argues_against": ["Cystic fibrosis", "Tuberculosis"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Spitting up or vomiting with feeds in infants", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Poor feeding with poor weight gain", "Choking or gagging with feeds", "Blood in vomit"], "argues_against": ["Gastroesophageal reflux with aspiration", "Tracheoesophageal fistula"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Itchy rash in the creases of the arms and legs", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Hives with a specific food", "Recurrent skin infections"], "argues_against": ["Food allergy as the only trigger"]}, {"system": "allergic_immunologic", "positives": [{"text": "Known allergies to dust, pets, or pollen", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Eczema", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Recurrent severe infections", "Reactions to vaccines"], "argues_against": ["Immunodeficiency"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "infants", "how_it_differs": "Infants cannot describe symptoms; they present with trouble feeding or sucking, rapid breathing, and irritability. Wheezing may be the only sign, and it can be hard to tell apart from bronchiolitis.", "missing_classic_features": ["Reported chest tightness", "Nighttime cough described by the child", "Spirometry"]}, {"population": "obesity", "how_it_differs": "Breathlessness with activity and reduced exercise tolerance are more prominent and may be attributed to weight rather than asthma, delaying diagnosis.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear-cut wheezing episodes"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Young children often cannot perform spirometry and may not report chest tightness; parents describe the symptoms instead. A trial of asthma medicine is sometimes used to support the diagnosis.", "missing_classic_features": ["Lung function testing", "Self-reported symptoms"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, playful, speaking in full sentences; may have mild tachypnea or audible wheeze at rest", "moderate": "Sitting upright, preferring not to lie flat; speaking in short phrases; visibly working to breathe; can feed but tires", "severe": "Tripod or upright posture, cannot speak in full sentences, agitated or drowsy, marked accessory muscle use, audible wheeze", "critical": "Exhausted, confused or lethargic, minimal air movement, may have paradoxical breathing; impending respiratory failure"}, "findings": [{"id": "audible-wheeze", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Listen with the stethoscope over the trachea and both lung fields during quiet breathing", "finding": "Expiratory wheezing, often musical or polyphonic, loudest on expiration", "frequency": "common", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "prolonged-expiration", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate and time the expiratory phase compared with inspiration", "finding": "Expiratory phase longer than inspiratory phase", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "accessory-muscle-use", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Observe the child's breathing for use of neck and intercostal muscles", "finding": "Suprasternal, supraclavicular, or intercostal retractions; nasal flaring; head bobbing in infants", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "tachypnea", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Count the respiratory rate for a full minute while the child is calm", "finding": "Respiratory rate above the normal range for age", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "hypoxemia", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure oxygen saturation with pulse oximetry on room air", "finding": "SpO2 below 95%", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "silent-chest", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate all lung fields", "finding": "Minimal or absent breath sounds with little wheeze despite severe distress", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "critical", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "cyanosis", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Inspect the lips, tongue, and nail beds", "finding": "Central or peripheral cyanosis", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "critical", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "normal-chest-wall", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Inspect and palpate the chest wall", "finding": "No focal asymmetry, no localized dullness or decreased breath sounds", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-stridor", "region": "neck", "maneuver": "Listen over the neck and trachea for inspiratory sounds", "finding": "No inspiratory stridor", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-fever", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure temperature", "finding": "Afebrile", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-heart-sounds", "region": "cardiac", "ma