 "Onset usually after age 40"], "exam": ["Barrel chest with decreased breath sounds", "Prolonged expiration that does not fully reverse with bronchodilators"], "labs": ["Spirometry shows obstruction with incomplete or no bronchodilator reversibility"], "imaging": ["Chest x-ray shows hyperinflation, flattened diaphragms, and increased retrosternal air space"]}}, {"name": "Pneumonia", "slug": "pneumonia", "why_considered": "Cough, dyspnea, and wheeze during an acute flare, especially when fever or purulent sputum is present", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Acute onset over hours to a few days with fever and chills", "Productive cough with purulent sputum", "Pleuritic chest pain"], "exam": ["Focal crackles, bronchial breath sounds, egophony, or dullness to percussion", "Fever and tachycardia"], "labs": ["Leukocytosis", "Elevated CRP or procalcitonin", "Positive sputum or blood cultures"], "imaging": ["Chest x-ray shows focal consolidation or infiltrate"]}}, {"name": "Pulmonary embolism", "slug": "pulmonary-embolism", "why_considered": "Acute dyspnea and chest discomfort that can be mistaken for an asthma flare", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Sudden dyspnea with pleuritic chest pain, tachycardia, unilateral leg swelling, or risk factors such as recent surgery, immobility, or prior VTE", "discriminators": {"history": ["Abrupt onset of dyspnea without a typical trigger", "Pleuritic chest pain", "Recent surgery, immobility, long travel, or prior clot", "Unilateral leg swelling or calf pain"], "exam": ["Tachycardia out of proportion to the lung exam", "Clear lungs despite marked dyspnea", "Signs of deep vein thrombosis"], "labs": ["Elevated D-dimer in low-risk patients", "Hypoxemia with a normal chest x-ray"], "imaging": ["CT pulmonary angiography shows filling defects in the pulmonary arteries"]}}, {"name": "Anaphylaxis", "slug": "anaphylaxis", "why_considered": "Acute wheeze and dyspnea after an allergen exposure, which can look like a severe