on differences or repetitive or restricted behaviors", "discriminators": {"history": ["Delayed or atypical language and social milestones", "Poor eye contact and difficulty reading social cues", "Repetitive movements or insistence on sameness", "Symptoms present from the first years of life, not just when school demands increase"], "exam": ["Atypical social reciprocity", "Repetitive or stereotyped movements", "Narrow, intense interests"], "labs": ["Genetic testing may be offered when dysmorphic features or developmental delay are present"], "imaging": ["Not routinely indicated"]}}, {"name": "Absence seizures", "slug": "absence-seizures", "why_considered": "Brief staring spells with loss of awareness can be mistaken for daydreaming and inattention", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Staring spells that interrupt activity, with no response during the spell and no memory of it afterward", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden brief staring spells lasting seconds, many times a day", "Activity stops and resumes abruptly", "No memory of the episode", "May have eyelid fluttering or lip smacking"], "exam": ["Normal between spells", "May be provoked by hyperventilation in the office"], "labs": ["No routine labs"], "imaging": ["MRI brain only if focal features or abnormal EEG localization"]}}, {"name": "Thyroid disease", "slug": "hyperthyroidism", "why_considered": "Restlessness, fidgeting, poor concentration and irritability can be caused by an overactive thyroid", "must_not_miss": false, "trigger": "Weight loss, heat intolerance, tremor, palpitations or poor growth despite good appetite", "discriminators": {"history": ["Weight loss despite increased appetite", "Heat intolerance and sweating", "Palpitations", "Symptoms are new rather than lifelong"], "exam": ["Tachycardia", "Fine tremor", "Goiter or eye findings"], "labs": ["Abnormal TSH with elevated free T4"], "imaging": ["Thyroid ultrasound or uptake scan only if a nodule or goiter is found"]}}, {"name": "Substance use", "slug": "substance-use-disorder", "why_considered": "Stimulant or cannabis use can cause restlessness, poor focus, declining school or work performance and irritability", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "A change from a stable baseline, new social circle, or physical signs of use", "discriminators": {"history": ["Symptoms began or worsened after starting a substance", "Use of stimulants, cannabis, alcohol or opioids", "Decline in function that tracks with use", "Drug-seeking behavior or withdrawal symptoms"], "exam": ["Signs of intoxication or withdrawal", "Nasal irritation or track marks", "Weight loss or poor hygiene"], "labs": ["Urine drug screen positive for the substance"], "imaging": ["Not indicated"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Symptoms are present but cause only minor difficulty; grades, friendships and family life are largely intact and the patient needs only monitoring, classroom accommodations or behavioral strategies", "moderate": "Symptoms clearly interfere with school, work or relationships; the patient needs a structured behavioral plan and usually medication, with regular follow-up", "severe": "Marked impairment across settings with failing grades, repeated discipline, lost jobs or strained relationships; needs combined behavioral and medication treatment with close follow-up and school or workplace support", "critical": "Severe impulsivity or agitation that puts the patient or others in immediate danger, such as running into traffic, self-injury or aggression requiring urgent behavioral management"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Suicidal ideation, self-harm or plan to hurt someone", "meaning": "Immediate safety risk; needs urgent mental health evaluation"}, {"finding": "Sudden onset of symptoms in an older adult with no childhood history", "meaning": "Look for another cause such as depression, medication effect, thyroid disease or cognitive impairment"}, {"finding": "Staring spells with loss of awareness", "meaning": "Possible absence sei