"any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Falls or fractures", "Burns or cuts from careless behavior"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "children", "differences": "Diagnosis depends on parent and teacher reports; preschool children present mainly with hyperactivity and tantrums, and behavioral therapy is first-line before medication."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "New attention problems in an older adult should prompt evaluation for depression, medication effects, sleep apnea and cognitive impairment rather than assuming ADHD."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Symptoms may become harder to manage with the demands of pregnancy and a new infant; treatment decisions must weigh fetal and breastfeeding safety, and stimulants are usually avoided or used cautiously."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Obesity is more common in people with ADHD and can worsen sleep apnea and daytime attention; weight and sleep should be addressed alongside ADHD treatment."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "When did you or your family first notice these problems?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Symptoms present since early childhood, before age 12, not a recent change"}, {"question": "Does this happen only at school, or also at home and with friends?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Symptoms in two or more settings, which is required for the diagnosis"}, {"question": "How long has this been going on?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "At least 6 months of persistent symptoms, not episodic"}, {"question": "Can you tell me about trouble paying attention or finishing tasks?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Careless mistakes, trouble sustaining attention, not seeming to listen, losing items, forgetting daily activities"}, {"question": "Do you fidget, get up when you are supposed to s