": "axillary lymph node ultrasound with fine needle aspiration", "why": "Confirms nodal involvement when nodes are clinically or radiographically abnormal", "only_if": "palpable or suspicious axillary lymph nodes"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Not a substitute for CT staging; rarely changes management", "only_if": "respiratory symptoms or an abnormal chest exam"}, {"test": "CA 15-3 or CA 27.29", "why": "Tumor markers are not used to diagnose or stage breast cancer"}, {"test": "CEA", "why": "No role in breast cancer diagnosis or staging"}, {"test": "d_dimer", "why": "No role in the workup of a breast mass"}, {"test": "procalcitonin", "why": "No role unless infection is suspected"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Not part of the breast mass workup"}, {"test": "lipase", "why": "Not indicated for a breast mass"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Not part of the diagnostic workup"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Not part of the diagnostic workup"}], "decision_points": ["Any solid breast mass in a woman over 30 is imaged first with diagnostic mammography and ultrasound, then sampled by core needle biopsy rather than excisional biopsy", "Pregnancy test before imaging, biopsy, or systemic therapy in anyone of childbearing potential", "Receptor status (estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, HER2) on the biopsy specimen drives systemic therapy and must be requested", "Axillary ultrasound with fine needle aspiration before sentinel node biopsy when nodes are clinically abnormal", "Staging imaging is reserved for locally advanced disease or symptoms; early-stage disease does not need routine CT or bone scan"], "criteria": [{"name": "BI-RADS assessment categories", "summary": "A standardized reporting scale for breast imaging: 0 needs additional imaging, 1 negative, 2 benign, 3 probably benign with short-interval follow-up, 4 suspicious and biopsy recommended, 5 highly suggestive of malignancy, 6 known biopsy-proven malignancy. Categories 4 and 5 prompt tissue sampling."}, {"